cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "OpenMassSpecCore: Shared record types and mzML writer for open Rust mass-spectrometry readers"
message: >
  If you use OpenMassSpecCore in your research, please cite it using the
  metadata below. Citation is encouraged and appreciated but not legally
  required.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Riley
    given-names: Nathan
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-1579-7312"
    website: "https://github.com/Sigilweaver"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Sigilweaver/OpenMassSpecCore"
url: "https://sigilweaver.app"
abstract: >
  OpenMassSpecCore is the shared foundation of the Sigilweaver open
  mass-spectrometry readers. It defines vendor-neutral spectrum, chromatogram
  and run records, the SpectrumSource trait every reader implements, a
  streaming mzML 1.1.0 writer with indexed output, typed PSI-MS controlled
  vocabulary terms, a profile-to-centroid transform and a conformance harness.
  A companion crate bridges the records to Apache Arrow. It is implemented in
  pure Rust with no dependency on vendor libraries.
license: "Apache-2.0"
license-url: "https://github.com/Sigilweaver/OpenMassSpecCore/blob/main/LICENSE"
date-released: "2026-11-27"
version: "4.0.0"
keywords:
  - mass spectrometry
  - proteomics
  - mzML
  - PSI-MS
  - Apache Arrow
  - bioinformatics
  - Rust
